{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Dressing the Part"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "A Tie That Matches"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 13}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts"}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": " Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Perfect Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect tense</span> to talk about something that will be complete by a certain time in the future. This is the past in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span>, you often refer to a time period. <br> For example: <br><span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"underline\">By this time next week</span>, you <span class=\"strong\">will have proven</span> to everyone that you are the best person for the job!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You often use the preposition <span class=\"italic\">by</span> with the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect</span>. <span class=\"italic\">By</span> means <span class=\"italic\">no later than</span> or can suggest the idea of progress up to a particular time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart for the form of the <span class=\"strong\">Future Perfect<span>:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"will + have + past participle\\\"}\",\"\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">will have chosen</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a tie.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "By this time next week, you will have proven to everyone that you are the best person for the job!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "By next week, I will have chosen a tie, at least."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I will have made a decision by then."}, {"type": "example", "content": "They will have hired me by the time I decide on a tie. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modals for Request: Could and Would "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "When you want to make polite requests you use indirect styles of speaking.  <br>The <span class=\"strong\">modal verbs</span> <span class=\"italic\">would</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> make requests more indirect."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Indirect speech is longer and wordier than direct speech "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Could</span> you tell me where the men's attire is, please? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> you be able to help me choose a tie? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Would</span> you please show me more red ties? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Could </span> you help me tie this tie?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example: <br> Direct = <span class=\"italic\">Where is the tie store?</span><br>Indirect = <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Could</span> you tell me where the tie store is?</span>  <br>&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp or<br>&nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp &nbsp <span class=\"italic\"> <span class=\"strong\">Would </span> you be able to tell me where the tie store is?</span>"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "fashion statement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "giving information about yourself from the clothes you choose to wear"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The color and design of your tie is more than just a fashion statement, it gives people insight into your attitude and personality."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le13ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text"